@junit | federation-latest-stored | 5 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 5
@junit | federation-latest-stored-next | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6
@junit | federation-latest-stored-since | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6
@junit | federation-latest-stored-muted | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1
@junit | federation-trending-kept-pulled | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6
# Posts from elsewhere a reader had on screen. Handing them over only fills memory, for a member
# or a signed-out device alike, and nobody's are turned away before anything is read. A flush
# writes everything held as one multi-row INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE. The latest without a
# reader key is the first read of memory as before (instance key, the chosen server's block, the
# post's server's block). With a device, each page read below asks once which of its posts the
# device saw before the scroll began: the unseen run (two reads, the second reaching the bottom)
# then the seen run from the top (one read); the next page reads once. The daily cleanup is one
# DELETE ... LIMIT while fewer than a batch are old enough.
@junit | federation-seen-latest-plain | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3
@junit | federation-seen | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0
@junit | federation-seen-member | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0
@junit | federation-seen-nobody | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0
@junit | federation-seen-flush | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1
@junit | federation-seen-latest-first | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3
@junit | federation-seen-latest-next | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1
@junit | federation-seen-cleanup | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2
# Posts from elsewhere ranked for the reader. A first page reads, for a member, their signals (likes,
# bookmarks, answers, followed accounts' notes and long dwells, with each note's author, language and
# tags, in one statement) and their language; then the kept notes of the last three days with the
# viewer's blocks, mutes, server blocks, language filter and follows applied, their tags, their
# counts, which of them the reader saw (with a reader key), and the page built as any note page
# (its notes by id, thread chain, remote authors, media, stats, a member's marks, and link cards
# when a note has an address). A later page is cut from the ranking held in memory, so it only
# builds its notes. A pool ten times wider costs what the first page did less its link cards. A
# dwell's flush finds its note by uri and writes it beside the sightings. A
# round of asking counts again reads the due notes, the server's block and the instance key, then
# writes every answer in one statement.
@junit | federation-for-you-anonymous | 9 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 9
@junit | federation-for-you-first | 13 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 13
@junit | federation-for-you-next | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6
@junit | federation-seen-dwell | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0
@junit | federation-seen-flush-dwell | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 3
@junit | federation-for-you-device | 11 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 11
